Analyze this {language} code for security misconfiguration (OWASP A05).

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- Debug, verbose or developer error pages reachable outside development
- CORS policies that accept any origin, header or method, especially with credentials
- Authentication or authorization globally disabled or bypassed by default
- Cookies without Secure, HttpOnly or a restrictive SameSite
- Missing security headers on responses (CSP, HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options)
- Containers or services running as root, privileged, or sharing host namespaces
- Default credentials, sample endpoints or admin consoles left enabled
- Services bound to every interface when a loopback bind would do
- Overly broad filesystem, bucket or IAM permissions

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "misconfig_type": "DEBUG_EXPOSED|PERMISSIVE_CORS|AUTH_DISABLED|INSECURE_COOKIE|MISSING_HEADERS|CONTAINER_PRIVILEGE|DEFAULT_CREDENTIALS|EXPOSED_BIND|BROAD_PERMISSIONS|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific misconfiguration",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
